Z||000004||Raydar||10-14-2001||01:12 AM||||If you can take the cover off the amp, you might be able to push the broken pin out from the inside. Straighten out a big paper clip and use it to poke the pin out of the jack.<BR>Did the same thing with a digital camera that had the tip of the serial cable broken off in the jack.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Pheagey||10-14-2001||10:07 PM||||   Yo thanks guy's. After about 5 hours cusin and restaning myself from putting the thing out my 5th floor window I did get it fixed. Next: speakers (any ideas were nfrom).<BR>   I took the cover off, cleaned out all the dirt/dust/silicon(sp?) out. I removed the RCA's outer sheilding (the L & R RCA plugs were combined) and was able to slide the male pin out.<BR>   thanks ||||reg||6
